#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221191 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af871f3d-da9e-5fd3-a61f-94e155ccf2b3" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "4874a486-2cf1-5b6e-ae4f-52579f03b077" :question/math-academy-id "e-21695" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9bdce761076544aff166409cc78bdf918c4afc2c47b67e6366e3aabb78087b7.png)\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions $\\mathbf x_1$ and $\\mathbf x_2,$ shown above. Find the fundamental matrix for the system." :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system $\\mathbf{x}' = A \\mathbf{x},$ where $A$ is an $n \\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $\\Phi(t)$ of the system is an $n \\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2 \\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}=[\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}=[\\begin{aligned}4t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 4{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n![](images/bb/bb710709a593f8d185cde601fb5082d7f79ed21af824c28949477d2011479d95.png)\n\n**Note:** The columns of $\\Phi$ can be written in any order."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221192 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221422 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"}] :question/id #uuid "3e053d6d-f051-5c4c-a20b-1e90b2d5941b" :question/math-academy-id "e-21696" :question/problem "![](images/81/819e3b9672e898801ef7320c1d80246d218ae89e76b3247c86b642a5f5790400.png)\nConsider the system of linear ODEs $\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x}$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix $\\Phi(t)$ for this system." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\mathbf x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system $\\mathbf x'(t) = A\\mathbf x(t),$ denoted $\\Phi_0(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\quad \\Phi_0(0)  = I_n,\n$$\n\nwhere $I_n$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & -7{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda) = \\alpha_1 \\lambda + \\alpha_0.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1 = 7\\textrm{i}t, \\qquad\n\\lambda_2 = -7\\textrm{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((7\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(7\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(7\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+7\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{7t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ into the expressions for the required entries of $e^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{7t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n![](images/4d/4d6fd69672291bf4c39d33a04656258b89a500bc039588a9fd27eb10db328cc3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221193 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "a52a6539-60d1-557c-a042-cbce5616e94f" :question/math-academy-id "e-21697" :question/problem "Consider the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2 \\times 2$ matrix. Let $\\Phi(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $\\Phi(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation $\\Phi'(t) = A \\, \\Phi(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $\\big[ \\mathbf{a}, \\: \\mathbf{b} \\big]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$*\n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\Phi(t) = \\big[ \\mathbf{x}_1(t), \\: \\mathbf{x}_2(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}_1'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}_1(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}_2'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}_2(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) = \\big[ \\mathbf{x}_1'(t), \\: \\mathbf{x}_2'(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) =  \\big[ A \\mathbf{x}_1(t), \\: A \\mathbf{x}_2(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) = A \\big[ \\mathbf{x}_1(t), \\: \\mathbf{x}_2(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) = A \\Phi(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L2}$ follows from the fact that ![](images/be/be39ec10432eb81c3e00fdf30599353450e1ae7ebebd136f20dce45deb685cac.png).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L6}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L5}$ by ![](images/09/09febb48bb00d22caebf088103181b5db6377befccad18f1370718351cc91e9d.png).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L7}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L6}$ and substitution from line ![](images/99/999db06dcfe0878ddb3316b11546668ba9442d8fd110165e5076b90964b84905.png)." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\textrm{L2}.$ Since $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns $\\mathbf{x}_1(t)$ and $\\mathbf{x}_2(t)$ are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t).$ This means that each column satisfies the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_1'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}_1(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L2}$ follows from the fact that $\\mathbf{x}_1$ is a solution of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\textrm{L5}$ and $\\textrm{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n\\Phi'(t)=\\big[A\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\:A\\mathbf{x}_2(t)\\big]\n= A\\big[\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\:\\mathbf{x}_2(t)\\big].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L6}$ follows from $\\textrm{L5}$ by factoring out $A$ on the left.\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L6}$ and $\\textrm{L7}.$ From $\\textrm{L6}$ we have $\\Phi'(t)=A\\big[\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\:\\mathbf{x}_2(t)\\big].$ Using $\\Phi(t)=\\big[\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\:\\mathbf{x}_2(t)\\big]$ from $\\textrm{L1},$ we substitute to obtain $\\Phi'(t)=A\\Phi(t).$ Thus, $\\textrm{L7}$ follows from $\\textrm{L6}$ by substitution from $L1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af871f3d-da9e-5fd3-a61f-94e155ccf2b3" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98445a5c-049c-54e6-96cf-219cb7c711ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220548} {:answer/id #uuid "3a595499-d50f-5403-bdf1-1362d27edc63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-e^{-2t} & 3e^{2t} \\\\ e^{-2t} & e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220549} {:answer/id #uuid "68f4ccfa-f931-505e-b8f9-acaaace9176e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220550} {:answer/id #uuid "75f2863c-5c04-5878-8281-aa0fffa67fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3e^{-2} & -e^{2} \\\\ e^{-2} & e^{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220551} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce5563f-2d8f-5752-82b0-fa34f60d301e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3e^{-2t} & -e^{2t} \\\\ e^{-2t} & e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220552}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6bff80bf-991a-5e44-9565-955b85bdc117" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220547}] :question/id #uuid "f190e3a4-5efc-5caa-a01f-c8d68875b312" :question/math-academy-id "q-333701" :question/problem "$x^{′} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x, x_{1}(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{-2t}, x_{2}(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{2t}$\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$, shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221422 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b62f64-a72a-58c3-83b7-f04a2c64a243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06b62f64-a72a-58c3-83b7-f04a2c64a243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305212} :answer-field/id #uuid "38ab63d4-df22-5b52-9665-41a9dd7da8dd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29616b45-1873-5c52-bde7-ea7fad263666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29616b45-1873-5c52-bde7-ea7fad263666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305540} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f8022a-afa7-5402-9578-ce5abfc3468c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1d6721b-ff98-5c3e-ad88-04c1ddec1e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d6721b-ff98-5c3e-ad88-04c1ddec1e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307378} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c6472ca-2c4e-5da6-9f5a-4788af95a430" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94eeb383-7b17-545d-8da7-02f82d01ed4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94eeb383-7b17-545d-8da7-02f82d01ed4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306553} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2155b73-1362-5f64-bf35-7930dcaeeb4a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ca7cf8a-29b9-5dc9-9eb7-2eb98441be57" :question/math-academy-id "q-333713" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((2\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+2\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e315641f-7048-5d22-999e-3be3cfc5af5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391266} {:answer/id #uuid "0233e06e-a302-51e4-b083-fe0aaa4725aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391267} {:answer/id #uuid "be3009e6-e7cf-57fb-8c1f-a885361311eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391268} {:answer/id #uuid "cf515a09-9dba-5d02-ae42-355ff706ce78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e315641f-7048-5d22-999e-3be3cfc5af5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391266} :answer-field/id #uuid "85305209-f127-50f4-8fb6-558c6f7e40e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391265} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a700d19b-464e-5807-9333-12ea7e2f2e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391271} {:answer/id #uuid "9667e6c0-3577-5729-b0b1-c1fd903f6823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}$ is a solution of the system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391272} {:answer/id #uuid "c43f1625-204a-5fc4-acbc-a60997cdf542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}$ is differentiable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391273} {:answer/id #uuid "27100933-11fb-5602-87aa-f18a23a2da08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9667e6c0-3577-5729-b0b1-c1fd903f6823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}$ is a solution of the system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391272} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a119ab6-43f8-5872-ab0c-26e93853cfdf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d630e396-6325-5e09-89df-19e69a52dddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391276} {:answer/id #uuid "63c0991b-ad6e-5f6a-98b8-643da1aae492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391277} {:answer/id #uuid "351118ef-d9b7-5b2c-8103-6248dbbc0401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating again" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391278} {:answer/id #uuid "cafa980d-badb-57fc-a8c3-a2ffc2a64bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d630e396-6325-5e09-89df-19e69a52dddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391276} :answer-field/id #uuid "155738af-3e2a-57a9-a635-a3db6456eb1e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49e5968a-1ea4-5510-81b8-9a383e60e6d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333719" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L4}$ and substitution from lines {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ This means that each column satisfies the differential equation. In particular, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that ${x}_{1}\\text{ is a solution of the system}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ By definition, the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column,\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}^{′}(t) & {x}_{2}^{′}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$ from $\\text{L3},$ we substitute each derivative into the matrix to get\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substitution from $\\text{L2}\\text{ and }\\text{L3}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}]=A[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}]=AΦ(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8335968c-9d4c-5fbb-9ffa-75dcaa53d606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220592} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b01ba2-8f40-5f19-b36b-a5bc0a007ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220593} {:answer/id #uuid "f95f3e3a-b149-5084-b607-3cd5fd0d18db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220594} {:answer/id #uuid "6493f73f-365f-5404-a5da-5e40752fbe4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220595}] :answer-field/id #uuid "93036466-1c3c-5e59-947c-e8ff8d157797" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8da938b1-3907-513f-b226-7d4a5fce6961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220597} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6e3f89-8339-5442-8b3b-4b61bf616f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220598} {:answer/id #uuid "45c1625c-895f-5835-8da3-f6ef1aaa3032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220599} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb2d3be-25c0-510e-baac-596049d86862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220600}] :answer-field/id #uuid "dccda4ab-5506-5030-89e0-e232b37f3a8b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "967d6780-0d69-5d91-b012-b91bfef745e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220602} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6e93eb-df3e-5bed-9de4-518f71241e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "\\Phi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220603} {:answer/id #uuid "e753d893-e42e-50d3-bb33-dac9396f5d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the zero factor theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220604} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa2aa18-1cb1-5685-99ca-77c79bd3efdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the properties of determinants" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220605} {:answer/id #uuid "50b95faa-9f24-5897-95ea-ffb54a1d3efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting $\\Phi' = A \\" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220606}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bdb71a74-1627-56af-a5ab-668a47e38b61" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220601}] :question/id #uuid "920ced52-32ff-52a3-a836-fb31a23c82e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-333722" :question/problem "Consider the system $x^{′}(t) = Ax(t)$, where $A$ is a constant $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n> $L1$: Let $x_{1}(t)$ and $x_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n> $L2$: $x_{1}(t)$ and $x_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n> $L3$: $det(Φ(t)) \\ne 0$ for all $t$\n> $L4$: $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nLine $L2$ follows from $L1$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\nLine $L3$ follows from line $L2$ by {{field-2}}.\n\nLine $L4$ follows from line {{field-3}} by the properties of invertible matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af871f3d-da9e-5fd3-a61f-94e155ccf2b3" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9dce11-9930-5ed8-a98a-71b2c6d613f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305731} {:answer/id #uuid "457fdc35-522e-54bf-b4a2-96a44738c939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305834} {:answer/id #uuid "6a690293-bc00-5f55-add0-38bfbd8cd231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306167} {:answer/id #uuid "d0722a55-c81c-5911-86e0-d5540fd6d7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2 & -{e}^{-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 \\\\ {e}^{-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 & {e}^{-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307079} {:answer/id #uuid "d321f46a-76a7-5be1-b689-e83b8deece3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c9dce11-9930-5ed8-a98a-71b2c6d613f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305731} :answer-field/id #uuid "034e9426-2cb9-545f-a8bf-8151560f1dcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e83b1a2-7579-5dd1-bddd-671f2c156572" :question/math-academy-id "q-334330" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221422 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cd42562-09cd-51eb-b4a2-b584bedeb569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cd42562-09cd-51eb-b4a2-b584bedeb569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365670} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0c533ef-5493-5cd1-a424-830212f48ffc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e04a12ae-abe9-59a0-b308-9184898a8572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e04a12ae-abe9-59a0-b308-9184898a8572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365672} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0b6879-e091-50fa-802c-bc06c1af37d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "162963ac-9899-549d-9b3f-b09605170db6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334389" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | ${e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ${e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t}$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-5t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=5t,\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(-5t)={e}^{-5t} \\\\ r(5t)={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-5t} \\\\ 5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-10t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{10t}({e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{10t}({e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t} & {e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t} & {e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c886e4d-ec71-526e-9fca-44411eb71087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396918} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee05532-dfb9-529e-b73c-929366f56b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396919} {:answer/id #uuid "1c690c80-9317-5e41-aaae-07f5c0248385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396920} {:answer/id #uuid "da083ae6-571f-54bb-bc13-27bab5c4d1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c690c80-9317-5e41-aaae-07f5c0248385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396920} :answer-field/id #uuid "319112f1-c5cd-5b59-bc98-0fbaa63699a8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f41205b8-acc0-5664-955b-74b059485116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396923} {:answer/id #uuid "82374921-7bf9-535e-9301-cd8fcd3d1de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the properties of determinants" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396924} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e658e-f066-597f-abf6-933f8b8713c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396925} {:answer/id #uuid "1a09ff54-d141-5e15-a5d8-b2bb7e05d498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e658e-f066-597f-abf6-933f8b8713c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396925} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c455c64-6a5a-53e9-8592-0cd96bbb254d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3dfad07-3750-584e-9f6f-d30755695967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396928} {:answer/id #uuid "995b3536-4529-5769-9f9a-f34c8177e004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396929} {:answer/id #uuid "dd384e88-52b2-55f6-8382-7ee54663a081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396930} {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931} :answer-field/id #uuid "f108e315-8611-579e-a41e-01f211239093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} {:answer/id #uuid "fe02d4db-11ef-5015-aea5-bf6b6e4b9f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396934} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1b6e19-58ed-5e2e-97f8-48746da9e753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7c7b3b-bbe4-57bb-8ae1-e9580b65ffd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fcd6208-dde9-5e8a-b2c1-ff9f0dade0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-336107" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from {{field-1}} by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}$ by the $\\text{the transitive property of equality}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019f61ec-0715-5cf3-adfc-318205b19d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308757} {:answer/id #uuid "1372a77a-5f40-583a-81b0-59907e180c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308888} {:answer/id #uuid "163f0f70-1745-5d82-a520-ee8ffbaf2c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308914} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb04a3e-77b8-5a44-b01c-eef493e8d810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309324} {:answer/id #uuid "938c8d2f-38c6-57b3-b2a9-b2bfb697728d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938c8d2f-38c6-57b3-b2a9-b2bfb697728d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309929} :answer-field/id #uuid "00d126dd-5882-5b53-ae52-aec393914e29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0b86ab-3623-5087-ad8d-f6d2bfda8ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308856} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccc770b-7d17-5822-a092-2b7e33126ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating again" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309332} {:answer/id #uuid "98050690-74a9-5e29-9fad-e82f13325cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309969} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4cdbf2-f24b-58f9-8cfd-d3356bc5f95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309991} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ec6680-ddc0-56bc-910c-473286d87036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb